<title>GERMANY: High grain yields in German North-Rhine Westphalia.</title>
<headline>High grain yields in German North-Rhine Westphalia.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's North-Rhine Westphalia state on Wednesday reported very high grain yields of 7.37 tonnes per hectare, which would be 4.8 percent higher than last year.</p>
<p>A statement from the state's statistics office said the result was preliminary, barring any negative weather impact on grain still in the fields, which included 25 percent of the winter wheat crop.</p>
<p>Harvest volumes were estimated at 4.25 million tonnes compared with 3.98 million in 1995, of which winter wheat was pegged at 2.13 million with an 8.48 tonnes/ha yield.</p>
<p>Expected yields of other grains were given as follows --</p>
<p>winter barley 6.54 tonnes/ha</p>
<p>triticale 7.05 tonnes/ha</p>
<p>rye 6.89 tonnes/ha</p>
<p>spring barley 5.39 tonnes/ha</p>
<p>oats 5.61 tonnes/ha</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
